/// Activates 1–25 of a campaign's assets as one ordered unit, and returns
/// a task to poll. Takes a **list** because the service owns the ordering.
/// Assets link to one another by URL — an email's call-to-action carries
/// the landing page's URL, the landing page's download field carries the
/// document's — and a URL does not exist until the asset it points at is
/// activated. Those edges are derived by the service from the campaign's
/// pinned template, so reconstructing and topologically sorting them is
/// work the service has already done, and getting it wrong arms an email
/// with a dead link. Name every asset you want live and the service
/// sequences them; "activate everything" is the list with every id in it,
/// which ListCampaignAssets already gave you. Asynchronous, because
/// activating an asset installs or arms behaviour that runs later and an
/// email activation bulk-loads its audience into the delivery platform.
/// Everything decidable **without** a write to the delivery platform is
/// evaluated before this returns; everything else lands on the task. A
/// refusal that applies to one asset does not fail the request: that asset
/// is on the task already FAILED, with its reason, and the rest run. A
/// refusal that applies to the whole request — a malformed list, an
/// unknown campaign, another task already running on this campaign, this
/// service's service-linked role being deleted (ConflictException
/// `SERVICE_LINKED_ROLE_DELETION_IN_PROGRESS`), a campaign setting an asset
/// in the request needs (ValidationException `CAMPAIGN_INCOMPLETE`), a
/// campaign sender that no longer passes `CreateCampaign`'s sender rules
/// while the request names an email (ValidationException with no
/// `FieldList`, whose message ends with one `Reason: ` token per failed
/// rule: `PATTERN_MISMATCH`, `SENDER_DOMAIN_NOT_ALLIANCE_LEAD`, or
/// `SENDER_DOMAIN_DKIM_MISSING` and/or `SENDER_DOMAIN_DMARC_MISSING`) —
/// is thrown, and nothing starts. One task runs on a campaign at a time. A
/// second concurrent call is refused with ConflictException /
/// CAMPAIGN_ACTIVATION_IN_PROGRESS, whose `ResourceId` names the task
/// already holding the campaign. Two tasks over *disjoint* asset sets are
/// refused too: the guard is deliberately campaign-wide, because
/// overlapping runs made the per-asset status misleading rather than merely
/// contended.
pub fn (c: Client) start_campaign_asset_activation_task(input: StartCampaignAssetActivationTaskRequest) -> StartCampaignAssetActivationTaskResponse ! StartCampaignAssetActivationTaskErr uses (net.dial, clock, rand) {
  let (ep, signing, extra) = c.route(endpoint_params_start_campaign_asset_activation_task(c.params, input)) ?? e => return Err(StartCampaignAssetActivationTaskErr.InvalidInput(e))
  var req = serialize_start_campaign_asset_activation_task(ep, input, rest.uuid(c.rand)) ?? e => return Err(StartCampaignAssetActivationTaskErr.InvalidInput(e))
  for h in extra {
    req.headers.push(h)
  }
  let resp = transport.send(c.transport, req, signing, restjson.classify) ?? e => return Err(StartCampaignAssetActivationTaskErr.Send(e))
  if resp.status >= 300 {
    return Err(deserialize_start_campaign_asset_activation_task_error(resp))
  }
  deserialize_start_campaign_asset_activation_task(resp) ?? e => Err(StartCampaignAssetActivationTaskErr.Deserialize(e))
}

