/// Starts an asynchronous task that packages a campaign's assets into a
/// single downloadable ZIP archive. Fire-and-return: the campaign is
/// validated (it must exist and not be cancelled), a task record is
/// persisted, an asynchronous execution is started, and the task id is
/// returned with status IN_PROGRESS. This operation does not inspect assets
/// — all resolution, exclusion, and failure are determined by the
/// execution and surfaced only by GetCampaignAssetExportTask. Every
/// campaign is exportable, including one never activated, because
/// renderable assets are composed on demand at export time rather than
/// requiring finished, launched deliverables.
